 "notes": [
  [
   "SAO++ edition of Adrian Studer's duckBATH (duckGLOW SAO, 2024, MIT).\\nHis CH32V003, boost converter, reverse-polarity FET,\\naddress jumpers and I2C pull-ups are replaced by the XIAO.",
   [
    134.62,
    101.6
   ]
  ],
  [
   "SW1: SAO = badge feeds the 3.3 V rail. OFF = XIAO D1 high\\n(through R4), firmware sleeps. USB-BAT = XIAO feeds the rail.\\nNever USB and SAO at once.",
   [
    134.62,
    113.03
   ]
  ],
  [
   "D1: common-anode RGB LED on the FRONT (the duck sits on it).\\nEach colour is lit by pulling its XIAO pin LOW (PWM):\\nred D10, green D8, blue D7. GPIO2 carries WS2812 data in;\\nSAO GPIO1 is not connected (the maker used it only to program his chip).",
   [
    134.62,
    124.46
   ]
  ]
 ]
}
